  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "The final was level at 1–1 after goals from Benzema and Mané. Zidane sent Bale on for Isco just after the hour, and within three minutes Real Madrid were in front."
    },
    {
      "label": "Build-up",
      "text": "Madrid moved the ball patiently through Modrić, Casemiro and Kroos, Ronaldo carried it forward on the left, and it came back inside before Marcelo was found free on the far flank."
    },
    {
      "label": "The technique",
      "text": "The cross arrived behind Bale, too awkward for a header or a normal volley. Bale leapt, turned away from goal and struck a left-footed overhead kick, keeping it down enough to hit the target."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "The shot flew into the top corner beyond Karius, who had no time to react from that range. Bale added a third from long range later as Madrid won 3–1."
    }
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "label": "Be sharp off the bench",
      "text": "Bale scores within minutes of coming on. A substitute should be ready to take the first chance, not ease into the game."
    },
    {
      "label": "Stretch, then cross",
      "text": "Patient play through the middle draws Liverpool's defenders in and leaves Marcelo free on the left with time to pick the cross."
    },
    {
      "label": "Improvise when awkward",
      "text": "The cross arrives behind Bale, where a header or a normal volley will not work. The overhead kick is what keeps it a first-time shot."
    },
    {
      "label": "Keep the overhead down",
      "text": "Meeting the ball high and striking through it keeps an overhead kick on target. Most end up over the bar because contact is made too low."
    }
  ],
